  "design": {
    "entrance": "A controlled orbit: the camera arcs around the cut-crystal title (yaw 55 deg and a slight pitch resolving to front-on) while hundreds of facets catch and lose the light.",
    "reveal": "On the impact frame the orbit settles, the display spotlight brightens and one star-shaped glint with a faint spectral fringe fires from a letter crown; facets keep scintillating gently.",
    "camera": "Measured orbit + dolly that decelerates into a locked front view; no shake.",
    "material": "Faceted crystal: Voronoi facet planes with per-facet specular flashes driven by the view angle, sharp flat chamfer bevel (crown), cool environment reflection, restrained dispersion (2-3 px RGB split on the brightest sparkles only).",
    "exit": "The title turns away in the opposite direction as the spotlight closes, leaving a last glint."
  },
  "fusion_notes": [
    "Facet scintillation in Fusion is approximated by a discontinuous FastNoise cell pattern clipped to the rendered title and modulated by the camera orbit; Text3D itself has smooth faces (no real facets).",
    "Dispersion is limited to a subtle tinted sweep; enable chromatic aberration in your grade if you want more prismatic separation (keep it restrained for readability)."
  ],
